        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-12T18:39:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I forgot `S0ix` is a substate of `S0` so technically we are still in `S0`, its enter/exit wont be called.\n\nSince S0ix is not part of architecture I think that in addition to `S0` enty/exit, we could either:\n1. keep `disable_sleep` \u0026 `disable_sleep` call in this function or\n2. call these functions on s0ix entry/exit\n\nNumber 2 would require to add same entry exit to every chipset handler (mtl, ptl, adl), this makes 1 more feasible.\n\n@keithshort@chromium.org, any comments?",
      "parentUuid": "c7ccd801_30fd0647",
